    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Sison-Glaz c-search solves nu(c) <= 1 - alpha < nu(c+1); the original code started at c=1 so the legitimate solution c=0 was unreachable when nu(1) exceeds 1 - alpha for very small n",
      "Edgeworth-based approximation nu(c) can be non-monotone and plateau below 1 - alpha for sparse counts; exact coverage is 1 once c >= n since the box [count - c, count + c] contains full support",
      "Fix in diff: nucp1 = nu(c + 1) if c + 1 < n else 1.0, substituting exact coverage 1 once c + 1 >= n",
      "Reference value from R MultinomialCI for zero-cell upper bound: 0.9655815875 (rebase discussion states 0.965582)",
      "Test vector [1,1,0,0,0,0,0] expected intervals: [0.5,1.0] for first two cells and [0.0, 0.9655815875] for remaining cells",
      "Original failure was raising generic Exception: Couldn't find a value for 'c'",
      "Method approximation documented as needing at least 7 categories with counts of about 5; resulting intervals are necessarily wide",
      "PR notes R's own implementation silently returns invalid intervals for the no-crossing case, so R was not usable as reference there"
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
